  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food Security Response South Kordofan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgtSave the Children International (SCI), in partnership with SKILLS for Nuba Mountains (SKILLs), is launching a comprehensive response to address the severe food crisis in Dilling, Dellami, Kao Abu Jubeheh, Tolodi and Heiban in the Two Areas targeting a total of 92,105 beneficiaries. Our integrated Nutrition (total beneficiariesnbspltbrgt51,484), Food Security and Livelihoods (FSL) (total beneficiaries 19,321), and WASH (total beneficaries 21,300) intervention targets vulnerable children under 5 and pregnant and breastfeeding women and girls (PBWG) during the hunger gap/lean season. The prioritized sectors and localities were a result of consultation meetings hosted by SHF, where all partners in the state helped determine the biggest needs. A total of ltbrgt92,105 direct beneficiaries will be targeted out of which approximately 62% are females. ltbrgtBuilding upon successful modalities implemented by the World Food Programme (WFP) and the Federal Ministry of Health (FMoH) of Sudan, our initiative entails a scale-up of proven strategies. This includes mass Mid-Upper Arm Circumference (MUAC) and edema screenings, adoption of the family MUAC approach, provision of cooking demonstrations, Social and Behavioral Change Communication (SBCC) sessions focusing on Infant and Young Child Feeding (IYCF), Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH), and health education, among others.lt/pgtltpgtThe distribution of agriculture inputs to vulnerable households, accompanied by training on best agricultural practices. Livestock support will also be extended to targeted households, coupled with refresher trainings for animal health workers. ltbrgtltbrgtThe projectnbsp faces the risk of exacerbating tensions and undermining social cohesion through discriminatory distribution of essential supplies. To mitigate this, prioritizing equitable resource allocation is crucial for fostering community trust and strengthening social bonds. Conducting thorough conflict analysis alongside other project assessments ensures interventions are tailored to address underlying tensions while effectively meeting life saving needs. See Annex on Conflict Sensitivity for more information how SC will adapt its response to address this.ltbrgtltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
